1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,839
Our project studies autonomous robot manipulation beyond a
successful grasp.

2
00:00:04,839 --> 00:00:12,581
Using a Franka Panda in MuJoCo, we ask where a complete pick-and-
place pipeline breaks, and which

3
00:00:12,581 --> 00:00:15,000
targeted changes recover the task.

4
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:22,212
The baseline loads six public YCB models and supports seeded random
object selection and placement.

5
00:00:22,212 --> 00:00:29,904
The robot proposes grasps, checks motion, closes its fingers, lifts,
transports and physically releases the object.

6
00:00:29,904 --> 00:00:33,750
We evaluate repeated randomized trials and retain failures.

7
00:00:33,750 --> 00:00:40,000
The object moves through simulated contact dynamics, without a
robot-object weld or teleportation.

8
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:46,207
Our modules separate observation, candidate generation, inverse
kinematics, collision checking and execution.

9
00:00:46,207 --> 00:00:54,483
Success requires an eighty-millimeter lift, one-second hold,
sustained bilateral contact, stable release and placement within
fifty-five

10
00:00:54,483 --> 00:00:55,000
millimeters.

11
00:00:55,000 --> 00:00:58,103
Clutter tests also limit neighbor displacement.

12
00:00:58,103 --> 00:01:03,793
Some observers use measured points, but planning still uses
simulator geometry.

13
00:01:03,793 --> 00:01:10,000
This is a controlled simulation study, rather than an end-to-end
real-camera system.

14
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:14,286
First, a nearby can blocks the robot's palm.

15
00:01:14,286 --> 00:01:18,571
The original candidates are safely rejected before motion.

16
00:01:18,571 --> 00:01:27,143
In the same scene, we append a bounded family of inclined and offset
grasps while preserving

17
00:01:27,143 --> 00:01:28,750
all collision checks.

18
00:01:28,750 --> 00:01:31,964
The new candidate completes the transfer.

19
00:01:31,964 --> 00:01:40,000
This development example illustrates the mechanism; the separate
paired experiment measures how often it helps.

20
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:45,625
Next, we replace the rigid target with a genuine three-dimensional
elastic solid.

21
00:01:45,625 --> 00:01:53,125
The controller measures normal force at both fingers and adjusts
bounded preload using the weaker contact.

22
00:01:53,125 --> 00:01:59,688
Fixed preload completes two of six soft-object tasks; force
regulation completes six of six.

23
00:01:59,688 --> 00:02:07,188
Under randomized rigid-object mass, friction and actuator delay,
completion changes from ten of twelve to twelve

24
00:02:07,188 --> 00:02:08,125
of twelve.

25
00:02:08,125 --> 00:02:13,750
However, average peak elastic strain increases from about three-
point-seven to four-point-nine percent.

26
00:02:13,750 --> 00:02:18,906
The result supports retention within the tested limits, not reduced
deformation.

27
00:02:18,906 --> 00:02:25,000
The force and strain curves shown here are from an illustrative
development run.

28
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:28,333
More observations do not automatically improve manipulation.

29
00:02:28,333 --> 00:02:34,048
We add missing stripes, drift, outliers and calibration bias to
synthetic depth.

30
00:02:34,048 --> 00:02:41,667
A single packet completes six of twelve tasks, while raw twenty-
four-packet fusion completes only one: accumulated

31
00:02:41,667 --> 00:02:44,048
outliers can distort foreground geometry.

32
00:02:44,048 --> 00:02:51,667
Requiring each voxel to receive support from three different packets
raises completion to nine of twelve.

33
00:02:51,667 --> 00:02:55,476
All remaining failures are wedge-shaped objects losing contact.

34
00:02:55,476 --> 00:03:03,095
The bottleneck moves from obtaining usable geometry toward retaining
the object, although shape and estimation effects

35
00:03:03,095 --> 00:03:05,000
are not separately isolated.

36
00:03:05,000 --> 00:03:12,467
For recovery, we inject a transient closure fault: the first
commanded opening remains wider than the

37
00:03:12,467 --> 00:03:12,933
target.

38
00:03:12,933 --> 00:03:16,667
Missing bilateral contact triggers a real grasp failure.

39
00:03:16,667 --> 00:03:22,267
The robot opens, performs a checked withdrawal, reobserves and
physically grasps again.

40
00:03:22,267 --> 00:03:26,933
The scene is initialized once and never reset between attempts.

41
00:03:26,933 --> 00:03:32,067
All six first attempts fail, and all six retry episodes succeed.

42
00:03:32,067 --> 00:03:39,533
This verifies recovery from the specified temporary fault, rather
than a universal recovery rate for natural

43
00:03:39,533 --> 00:03:40,000
failures.

44
00:03:40,000 --> 00:03:46,897
Additional studies carry a freely hinged assembly and estimate
grasps for procedural objects without supplying target

45
00:03:46,897 --> 00:03:47,328
CAD.

46
00:03:47,328 --> 00:03:50,776
The shape methods tie at eleven of twelve.

47
00:03:50,776 --> 00:03:57,672
In stronger clutter, active observation actually falls from five of
six to three of six because

48
00:03:57,672 --> 00:03:59,397
of additional placement failures.

49
00:03:59,397 --> 00:04:05,000
We keep these unfavorable results instead of presenting every
extension as an improvement.

50
00:04:05,000 --> 00:04:08,987
The candidate study contains one hundred eighty physical episodes.

51
00:04:08,987 --> 00:04:16,076
Local alternatives change completion from fifty-four to fifty-eight
out of sixty with three neighbors, and from

52
00:04:16,076 --> 00:04:19,620
twenty-six to twenty-nine out of thirty with five.

53
00:04:19,620 --> 00:04:23,608
The exploratory study separately contains one hundred twenty-six
episodes.

54
00:04:23,608 --> 00:04:28,924
We pair initial scenes and physics, preserve failures and report
confidence intervals.

55
00:04:28,924 --> 00:04:32,025
No comparison passes its stated statistical threshold.

56
00:04:32,025 --> 00:04:39,114
Development footage is excluded from these denominators, and the two
studies are never pooled into one

57
00:04:39,114 --> 00:04:40,000
success rate.

58
00:04:40,000 --> 00:04:46,522
Our main finding is that geometry, observation quality and contact
retention must be evaluated together.

59
00:04:46,522 --> 00:04:52,174
The deliverables include runnable source, frozen records, a ten-page
report and reproduction instructions.

60
00:04:52,174 --> 00:04:55,217
Forty-nine tests and both evidence audits pass.

61
00:04:55,217 --> 00:05:00,000
Future work targets wedge stability, deformation-aware control and
less ideal sensing.
